# Single open runtime profile for the iSCSI local sanity flow.
#
# The four connection settings below are governed by the runtime-profile
# contract (tests/sanity/local/runtime-profile.sh): the local sanity entry
# points (tests/sanity/run.sh local and tests/run-all-tests.sh sanity local)
# select ONE open profile source explicitly and FAIL preflight when it is
# missing or partial. There are no silent defaults and no fallback channel
# that scrapes documentation.
#
#   * FILE MODE — if config.env EXISTS, it is authoritative for the four
#     STORAGE_* connection keys: it must provide all four on its own, with
#     literal values. It is evaluated with the environment cleared for these
#     keys, so ${VAR:-} template lines inherit NOTHING — fill each with a
#     literal value or preflight rejects the file as partial.
#   * ENV MODE — if config.env DOES NOT EXIST, all four keys must be present
#     and non-empty in the exported environment.
#
# Do not mix a partial config.env with inherited environment values: the run
# is refused before any live access.
#
# Limitation: the preflight checks that the four fields are present and
# non-empty from one source. It does NOT verify that the credential,
# endpoints, pool and portal group all belong to the SAME storage array —
# confirm that yourself; only the live runtime proves it.
#
# Copy to config.env and fill in literal values for this test environment.
# config.env is ignored by Git; supply the credential at runtime or only in
# the ignored file.
STORAGE_IPS=""
STORAGE_POOL_NAME=""
STORAGE_API_KEY=""
STORAGE_PORTAL_GROUP=""

# The local controller currently requires Kubernetes Lease coordination.
# These describe an existing pod identity and pre-created Lease domain; do not
# invent values or use a production domain for an independent test process.
# They are loaded from this file or the exported environment by the
# dispatcher's config source; they are NOT part of the validated four-key
# runtime profile above.
NGX_COORDINATION_LEASE_PREFIX="${NGX_COORDINATION_LEASE_PREFIX:-}"
POD_NAMESPACE="${POD_NAMESPACE:-}"
POD_NAME="${POD_NAME:-}"
POD_UID="${POD_UID:-}"
# Block drivers also require KUBE_NODE_NAME for node-role coordination.
KUBE_NODE_NAME="${KUBE_NODE_NAME:-}"